-- C29 example: two-way phase-field fracture growth (HFGROW ... PHASEFIELD eta TWOWAY).
-- Same layer and fracture as HFGROW_PHASEFIELD.DATA, slower injection (1 sm3/d). The first phase-field step uses the
-- eta volume; afterwards the crack volume follows the flow model (V = compliance x (fracture pressure - closure), capped by
-- the water injected in the step) and every fracture piece gets the cubic-law conductance of the Sneddon aperture of the
-- phase-field crack. Compare with the one-way run (remove TWOWAY): the one-way crack stays short while the flow-model
-- fracture pressure stays above the LEFM pressure. Results: Faults & seismicity -> Phase field (note 'two-way').
-- Expected (CLI ~55 s): half-length ~33 m after 88 days, phase-field crack pressure 34.11 MPa vs flow-model 34.18 MPa.
